<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Autariatae</h1><p class="st-meta">450 BCE – 230 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Large Illyrian tribal people of the central Balkans who overpowered the Triballi before being broken by Celtic invaders and Macedon.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Autariatae lived in the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drina">Drina</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lim-river">Lim</a> valleys, in modern western <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/serbia">Serbia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/montenegro">Montenegro</a>, by the 5th century BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a> calls them once the greatest and best of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illyrians">Illyrians</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known of their government; they appear as a warrior people of the interior. They fought their neighbours the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardiaei">Ardiaei</a> over salt springs, and in the 4th century BCE defeated the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/triballi">Triballi</a> and pushed east.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 310 BCE Celtic incursions and a plague weakened them, and the Macedonian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cassander">Cassander</a> resettled some 20,000 of them near Mount Orbelus. Their remnants were absorbed by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/scordisci">Scordisci</a> and other neighbours, and the name disappears in the 3rd century BCE.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/autariatae.jpg" alt="Autariatae" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: Dirgela · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Taros_kanjonas.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>450 BCE – 230 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Illyrian polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Illyrian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/serbia">Serbia</a>, <a href="/countries/bosnia-and-herzegovina">Bosnia and Herzegovina</a>, <a href="/countries/montenegro">Montenegro</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Autariatai</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-340&amp;focus=autariatae" aria-label="Autariatae on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5178 614 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Autariatae lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5498 870h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5498 870h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Serbia. <a href="/atlas?year=-340&amp;focus=autariatae">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

